# /etc/keel/sqlite -- one SQLite database path per line, absolute.
#
# Each is snapshotted daily with `VACUUM INTO` (consistent, compacted, only a
# read transaction so writers are not blocked for long) into /var/lib/keel/dumps,
# which is inside the backup scope.
#
# Every path listed here is ALSO added to borg's exclude list, along with its
# -wal and -shm siblings. That is the point of declaring them: a live SQLite
# file must never be read directly by borg, and this manifest is what guarantees
# it. The exclusion is automatic -- do not also list them in `exclude`.
#
# Empty by default. A VM that declares nothing dumps nothing and says so in the
# journal.
#
# Example:
# /var/lib/lodestone/lodestone.db
